    "content": "The baseline specification is drafted. **This is the first SDD gate — please review it before we plan or write any code.**\n\n## 📄 Spec ready for review\n\n- **Feature directory:** `specs/001-bookmark-manager/`\n- **Spec file:** `specs/001-bookmark-manager/spec.md`\n- **Quality checklist:** all items pass (`checklists/requirements.md`)\n\n### What the spec proposes — a bookmark manager, built in priority slices\n\n| Priority | User story | In short |\n|----------|-----------|----------|\n| **P1** | Save a bookmark | Enter an address (+ optional title), it's validated and saved |\n| **P1** | Browse & open | See your list, click to open the original page |\n| **P2** | Edit & delete | Fix or remove bookmarks, with a delete confirmation |\n| **P3** | Find & organize | Search by keyword, tag bookmarks, filter by tag |\n\nIt also covers edge cases (duplicate links, missing `http://`, very long titles, big collections) and sets measurable success criteria (e.g. save your first bookmark in under 30 seconds, no data loss across reloads, responsive with 500+ bookmarks).\n\n### ⚠️ Key assumptions I made — please confirm\n\nRather than block on questions, I chose reasonable defaults and documented them. The important ones:\n\n1. **Single user, personal use** — no accounts, sign-in, or sharing. *This is the biggest scope call.* If you meant a multi-user or shared product, tell me now — it changes a lot.\n2. **Web app** in the browser — no native mobile/desktop app or browser extension in v1.\n3. **Local persistence** — bookmarks survive reload on the same device; no cross-device sync in v1.\n4. **Manual entry** — no auto-import from a browser and no automatic page-title/thumbnail fetching in v1.\n5. **http/https links only.**\n\n### 👉 Your move at this gate\n\n- **Looks good?** Say so and I'll proceed to `speckit-plan` (the implementation plan) — still no code until you approve that too.\n- **Want changes?** Tell me what's wrong or missing and I'll revise the spec.\n- **Want me to probe ambiguities first?** I can run `speckit-clarify` for structured questions before planning.\n\nI'll wait for your confirmation before moving on.",
