    "content": "The revised specification is ready. **Still at the spec-review gate — please review before we plan.**\n\n## 📄 Revised spec — `specs/001-bookmark-manager/spec.md`\n\nI folded in everything you described and reversed the two earlier assumptions that conflicted with it. Here's what changed and what's now covered, as prioritized user stories:\n\n| Priority | Story | Now includes |\n|----------|-------|--------------|\n| **P1** | Save a link with auto-details | Auto-fetch **title, description, favicon, preview image**; edit title/description; **duplicate → open existing bookmark, no duplicate** |\n| **P1** | Browse & open | Normal list shows **title, description, tags, favicon**; open in new tab |\n| **P2** | Organize | **Note**, multiple **tags** (with suggestions from tags you already use), **unread/read-later**, **archive**; separate **unread** and **archived** views; archived hidden from normal browsing/search |\n| **P2** | Search precisely | Case-insensitive across **title/description/note/address**; **`#tag`**, **exact phrases**, **AND/OR/NOT + parentheses**; **sorting** |\n| **P3** | Bulk actions | Multi-select bulk changes **and** \"apply to everything matching the current view\" |\n| **P3** | Saved searches | Name, reopen, rename, delete a query+filters+sort |\n| **P3** | Snapshots & Internet Archive | Local page snapshot (**PDF kept as PDF**); submit to **Internet Archive** and record the link |\n| **P3** | Import/export | **Netscape bookmark-file** import and export |\n| **P3** | Display preferences | Default **sort**, **items shown**, **font size**; persisted |\n\nBacked by **34 functional requirements** (FR-001–034), an expanded **Key Entities** set (Bookmark, Tag, Saved Search, Snapshot, Display Preferences), edge cases (partial/slow metadata, PDF targets, invalid boolean expressions, Internet Archive unavailable, low local storage), and measurable success criteria including \"duplicate opens existing in 100% of cases,\" \"archived appears in 0% of normal results,\" and \"exported Netscape file re-imports into a mainstream browser.\"\n\n### A few notes for your review\n\n- **Assumptions updated:** automatic metadata capture and browser import/export are now marked **in scope** (previously excluded). Single-user browser app, same-device storage, and http/https-only remain as you confirmed.\n- **Snapshots/Internet Archive** depend on the target page and the archive service being reachable — the spec treats failures as recoverable rather than blocking the bookmark.\n- I kept it technology-agnostic (no framework/storage decisions) — those belong in the plan.\n\n### 👉 At this gate\n\n- **Approve** and I'll proceed to `speckit-plan` (still no code until you approve the plan too).\n- **Want changes** to scope, priorities, or any requirement? Tell me and I'll revise.\n- **Want structured clarifying questions first?** I can run `speckit-clarify`.\n\nI'll wait for your go-ahead.",
