    "content": "The implementation plan and its design artifacts are ready. **This is the plan-review gate — please review before I generate tasks or write any code.**\n\n## 📐 Plan ready — `specs/001-bookmark-manager/plan.md`\n\n**Artifacts:** `plan.md`, `research.md` (12 decisions), `data-model.md`, `contracts/` (api, search-grammar, netscape-format), `quickstart.md`. Constitution file is an unfilled template, so there are no ratified project gates; I held the plan to the method's baseline (spec-first, simplicity, testability) — it passes with no complexity to justify.\n\n### The core architectural decision — why there's a server\n\nThree features you approved **can't** be done by a browser alone, because browsers block cross-origin reads of other sites (CORS):\n- **auto-metadata** (fetch the page's title/description/favicon/preview),\n- **self-contained HTML snapshots** (fetch the page + all its resources),\n- **Internet Archive saving** (cross-origin POST to archive.org).\n\nSo the app is **one local Node process** that serves the UI *and* a small API on port 4000, with all data stored **on your device**. \"Same-device storage\" is preserved — the server and its database live on the same machine you run the app on.\n\n### Proposed stack\n\n| Layer | Choice | Why |\n|-------|--------|-----|\n| Server | **Node.js 24 + Express** | Provided by the runtime; serves UI + API on `0.0.0.0:4000` via `npm start` |\n| Storage | **SQLite (better-sqlite3)** + filesystem for snapshots/images | Single-user, same-device, no separate service; handles 500+ easily |\n| UI | **React + Vite** (built, served by the server) | Rich interactions: live search, bulk select, tag-suggest, Markdown preview |\n| Metadata | server fetch + **cheerio**; async (`pending`→`complete/failed`) | Non-blocking saves |\n| Snapshots | **Playwright 1.61.0 / Chromium** (already installed) → self-contained HTML; PDFs passed through | Reuses the pinned browser; no second download |\n| Notes | **marked + DOMPurify** | Safe Markdown rendering |\n| Search | hand-written tokenizer + parser | Needed for `#tag`+boolean+phrase+literal-when-quoted rules |\n| Tests | **node:test** (unit) + **Playwright** (E2E) | Cover risky logic + journeys |\n\n### What the design artifacts pin down\n\n- **data-model.md** — tables for bookmark, tag (unique `name_key` enforcing your single-identity rule FR-008a), bookmark_tags join, saved_search (include/exclude tags), snapshot (html/pdf), preferences singleton; plus state transitions (metadata, archive⇄, read⇄, permanent delete).\n- **contracts/api.md** — every endpoint, incl. duplicate-returns-existing on POST, bulk \"apply to all matching,\" snapshot capture/serve, archive-org, import/export.\n- **contracts/search-grammar.md** — full EBNF + evaluation table + worked examples (`#js promise` = both required; `\"AND\"` = literal).\n- **contracts/netscape-format.md** — field mapping preserving address, title, **tags, and ADD_DATE**; whole-file rejection on malformed input.\n\n### A couple of choices worth your explicit nod\n\n1. **Local server** (vs. a pure browser app) — required for the reasons above. Still single-user, same-device, no accounts.\n2. **Tag identity is case-insensitive** — so `News` and `news` are one tag (prevents near-duplicates, matches case-insensitive search). Say if you'd rather tags be case-sensitive.\n3. **Favicon + preview images cached locally** on save (best-effort) so the list works offline and survives link rot.\n\n### 👉 At this gate\n\n- **Approve** and I'll run `speckit-tasks` to produce the dependency-ordered task breakdown (I'll bring that back too before implementing).\n- **Want changes** to the stack or any design choice? Tell me and I'll revise the plan.\n\nI'll wait for your go-ahead.",
