    "content": "Plan updated. **Back at the plan-review gate.**\n\n## 📐 Plan updated — delayed-metadata safeguard added\n\nYour three confirmations are already baked in (local helper process, case-insensitive tags so `News` = `news` per R9, local image caching per R5). The new safeguard is now explicit across the artifacts as **research decision R13**:\n\n**The rule:** automatic details fill **only fields you haven't customized**, and can never overwrite a title/description you entered — whether you typed it while saving or edited it *while the fetch was still running*.\n\n**How it's guaranteed (not just intended):**\n- Each bookmark carries `title_user_set` / `description_user_set` flags (**data-model.md**). Supplying or editing the field — at save or later — sets its flag.\n- The async metadata worker uses a **conditional write** — `UPDATE ... SET title=? WHERE id=? AND title_user_set=0` — so a fetch that finishes *after* your edit simply no-ops on that field. This closes the race you're worried about, without locking. Favicon/preview (no user-entered form) still fill normally.\n- **Tested explicitly**: a unit test simulates a metadata fetch resolving *after* a user edit and asserts the user's value survives, plus an E2E check. Recorded in the Constitution Check's testability note, **quickstart.md** story 1, and the `npm test` description.\n\nUpdated files: `research.md` (R13), `data-model.md` (flags + race-safe transition + validation rule), `plan.md` (constraint + testability), `contracts/api.md` (safeguard note), `quickstart.md` (validation step + unit-test note).\n\n### 👉 At this gate\n\n- **Approve** and I'll run `speckit-tasks` for the dependency-ordered breakdown (brought back before implementing).\n- **More changes?** Tell me.\n\nI'll wait for your go-ahead.",
