    "content": "The task, its tests, and the API contract are updated and consistent. **Back at the tasks-review gate.**\n\n## ✅ Tasks updated — \"apply to all matching\" now respects the whole view\n\nThe fix makes the bulk selection carry a full **view descriptor**, not just search words, so it can never reach outside what you're actually looking at.\n\n**T039 (endpoint)** — `select.matchView` is now `{ view, q, tag, includeTags, excludeTags, sort }` (the same fields as the list endpoint). The server resolves it through the **same query + search-evaluator path as `GET /api/bookmarks`**, honoring **every** facet — view scope (normal/unread/archived), a clicked tag filter, a saved search's include/exclude tags, and the search expression — and **ignoring pagination**. So the affected set is exactly the complete current result set across all pages, and nothing outside it.\n\n**T040 (frontend)** — \"apply to all matching\" sends the **exact active view descriptor**, never a bare `q`.\n\n**Tests strengthened:**\n- **T038 (E2E)** — now runs \"apply to all matching\" over a view that *combines* a scope (unread/archived) + clicked tag filter + saved-search include/exclude tags + search words, **spanning more than one page**, and asserts every matching item (including on later pages) changes while every non-matching bookmark (wrong scope, excluded tag, non-match) is untouched.\n- **T038a (new unit test)** — verifies the server rebuilds the match set from the full descriptor identically to the list query and ignores pagination.\n\n**Also updated:** `contracts/api.md` bulk section now specifies this descriptor and states that sending a bare `q` without the rest of the active view is a client error.\n\nUS5 now has 4 tasks (T038, T038a, T039, T040); total **63 tasks**. All other phases unchanged.\n\n### 👉 At this gate\n\n- **Approve** and I'll begin implementation with `speckit-implement` (MVP first: Setup → Foundational → US1).\n- **More changes?** Tell me.\n\nI'll wait for your go-ahead before writing any code.",
